# Unit tests (`%testharness-live`)

Same suite shape as `examples/unittests.wcn`, but for the **live** interpreter.
Schema + Methods library; Target embeds many constructions via `%with`.

In the Play wiki, open this page and press **Run** — results appear as a
PASS/FAIL report (no canvas or CLI loop).

## Schema

```
Rect = Int/w Int/h
Point = Int/x Int/y
```

## Methods

```
Rect::area = { w * h }

Rect::contains = { Point/p |
  (p.x >= 0) and (p.x < w) and (p.y >= 0) and (p.y < h)
}

Point::moved = { Int/dx, Int/dy | [:Point (x + dx) (y + dy)] }
```

## Target

```
%testharness-live

%with
[:Rect 10 20]

%assert
"area of 10x20"
rect.area() == 200

"origin is inside"
rect.contains(new Point(0, 0)) == true

"far corner is outside"
rect.contains(new Point(10, 20)) == false

%with
[:Rect 3 4]

%assert
"area of 3x4"
rect.area() == 12

%with
[:Point 5 7]

%assert
"moved right"
point.moved(3, 0).x == 8

"moved up"
point.moved(0, -2).y == 5
```
